  - Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct, Alibaba Cloud: the text encoder layers, the token embedding table and the tokenizer
    model: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct (revision ebb281ec70b05090aa6165b016eac8ec08e71b17)

Changes made to those works:
  - The PyTorch models were converted to LiteRT (.tflite) graphs with litert-torch: the Qwen3-VL-4B text
    decoder (layers 1-35, text only) as 12 graphs, the iris-3b Turbo text adapter and diffusion transformer as
    8 graphs. The fully-connected weights are stored as fp16; all other tensors are fp32.
  - Host-side tensors (rotary tables, the timestep embeddings and modulation rows of the fixed 4-step schedule,
    the step sigmas, a reference starting noise) were computed from the upstream model and stored in
    iris_host.f32; the token embedding table is stored as raw bf16 in iris_embed_bf16.f32; the tokenizer tables
    and the chat-template ids are stored in iris_tokenizer.json.
  - python/ and android/ are new code that runs these files.

